=== (8) GOTCHAS ===
(a) `buildRecord` (:1336) expands `spec.validation_commands` into the WORKER'S BASH GRANTS (record.mjs:516). The floor sits above that — a spec with a wrong-typed `validation_commands` can no longer reach grant expansion for an executor. Worth a sentence in your gate comment; it is the security framing of this slice.
(b) The `failures[]` details come from spec-lint's `${v.path}: ${v.message}`, and this repo's validator interpolates the offending value into the message. That is acceptable HERE (the dispatch JSON goes to the orchestrator's own stdout, and the spec is a lead-authored file the orchestrator already reads) but it is why the refusal MESSAGE itself is a fixed, parameterless constant with nothing interpolated — do not add the failing field names or values to the message.
(c) The suite spawns real fake-cmux subprocess topologies; `node --test test/cmux-dispatch.test.mjs` takes tens of seconds. That is normal, not a hang. One flake under heavy concurrent load was observed during issue #19 — re-run before reporting a failure.
